t":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.14668866868511904,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":73.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.23385296499875843,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.14722288666270755,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.08309820764252507,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":66.5,"_gate_margins":-0.0014677635772359365,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":48.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.10899269586433018,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.046018058075396884,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":62.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.002344806174589875,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":47.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.017549582046214752,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":70.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.01681,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SandRidge Energy, Inc. engages in the acquisition, development, and production of oil and natural gas in the United States Mid-Continent region. As of December 31, 2025, it holds interests in 1,446 gross (825 net) producing wells, and one active drilling rig. The company was incorporated in 2006 and is based in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Grayson R. Pranin Jr. | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $716,113 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 102 people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue falling 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $407K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $27K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["SandRidge Energy, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $484M market cap on $156M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -15% over the past three years and -15% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +23.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.43\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 11% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 23% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 52% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"There May Be Underlying Issues With The Quality Of SandRidge Energy's (NYSE:SD) Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-sd/sandridge-energy/news/there-may-be-underlying-issues-with-the-quality-of-sandridge","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794568704.106,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"SandRidge Energy upgraded at Freedom Broker on production growth